IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sga-time`
IMPORT `sga-part2`
IMPORT `sga-part3a`
IMPORT `sga-part3b`

-- sga-tests-part3b.l4: worked cases for sga-part3b.l4. Expected values are hand-written from sections 16B, 18C, 18D, 19 to 20D and 30.

`no holidays` MEANS EMPTY

§ `Section 18C(1): the contributions that count for the QE day`

-- QE day 1 July 2026. Received 5 July (usual period, 100), 15 June 2026 (12-month period, 200), 20 July (outside both, 300), 30 June 2025 (before the 12-month period, 400).
`four contributions` MEANS LIST (`Eligible contribution received` OF 100, Date 5 7 2026), (`Eligible contribution received` OF 200, Date 15 6 2026), (`Eligible contribution received` OF 300, Date 20 7 2026), (`Eligible contribution received` OF 400, Date 30 6 2025)
#ASSERT `the total of the eligible contributions received in the periods for the QE day` (Date 1 7 2026) `no holidays` NOTHING `four contributions` EQUALS JUST 300
-- With an applicable table item ending 29 July 2026: 20 July now counts, and so does 30 June 2025 (the text puts no start on "before the end of the latest day").
#ASSERT `the total of the eligible contributions received in the periods for the QE day` (Date 1 7 2026) `no holidays` (JUST (Date 29 7 2026)) `four contributions` EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `the total of the eligible contributions received in the periods for the QE day` (Date 1 7 2026) `no holidays` NOTHING EMPTY EQUALS JUST 0
-- QE day 29 February 2028: a contribution on 28 February 2027 cannot be placed.
#ASSERT `the total of the eligible contributions received in the periods for the QE day` (Date 29 2 2028) `no holidays` NOTHING (LIST (`Eligible contribution received` OF 100, Date 28 2 2027)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the total of the eligible contributions received in the periods for the QE day` (Date 29 2 2028) `no holidays` NOTHING (LIST (`Eligible contribution received` OF 100, Date 1 3 2027)) EQUALS JUST 100

§ `Section 18C(1) and 18D: the base and final shortfalls`

#ASSERT `the individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall` 1200 500 EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `the individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall` 1200 1200 EQUALS 0
-- Paragraph (d): the contributions applied cannot take the amount below nil.
#ASSERT `the individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall` 1200 1500 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall` 1200 0 EQUALS 1200
-- 18D(2): latest day 10 July 2026, assessment on 20 July 2026: the late period is 11 to 19 July. 300 on 10 July and 50 on 20 July are outside it.
`late contributions` MEANS LIST (`Eligible contribution received` OF 300, Date 10 7 2026), (`Eligible contribution received` OF 200, Date 11 7 2026), (`Eligible contribution received` OF 100, Date 19 7 2026), (`Eligible contribution received` OF 50, Date 20 7 2026)
#ASSERT `the total of the eligible contributions received during the late period` (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 20 7 2026) `late contributions` EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `the total of the eligible contributions received during the late period` (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 20 7 2026) EMPTY EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall` 700 300 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall` 0 300 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall` 700 800 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall` 700 700 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall` 700 0 EQUALS 700

§ `Section 19A: the individual notional earnings component`

-- Base 1000 and a rate of 1 per cent a day for two days: 10, then (1000 + 10) x 1 per cent = 10.1; 20.1 in all.
#ASSERT `the notional earnings for the days` 1000 (LIST 0.01, 0.01) EQUALS 20.1
#ASSERT `the notional earnings for the days` 1000 EMPTY EQUALS 0
-- A final shortfall greater than nil: every day of the late period counts. Two days and two rates.
#ASSERT `the individual notional earnings component` 1000 400 2 (LIST 0.01, 0.01) EQUALS JUST 20.1
-- A final shortfall of nil: no day counts.
#ASSERT `the individual notional earnings component` 1000 0 2 (LIST 0.01, 0.01) EQUALS JUST 0
-- The list of rates does not match the number of days: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `the individual notional earnings component` 1000 400 3 (LIST 0.01, 0.01) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 19B: the administrative uplift amount`

-- 60% of (1000 + 100) = 660; reduced by 100 under the regulations = 560; a reduction larger than the amount leaves nil.
#ASSERT `the administrative uplift amount` 1000 100 0 EQUALS 660
#ASSERT `the administrative uplift amount` 1000 100 100 EQUALS 560
#ASSERT `the administrative uplift amount` 1000 100 660 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the administrative uplift amount` 1000 100 700 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the administrative uplift amount` 0 0 0 EQUALS 0

§ `Sections 20 to 20D: the choice loading`

#ASSERT `Subdivision E applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Subdivision E applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Subdivision E applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Subdivision E applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `section 20D applies to a contribution not made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`section 20D applies to a contribution not made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 20D applies to a contribution not made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 20D applies to a contribution not made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 20D applies to a contribution not made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 20D applies to a contribution not made in compliance with the choice of fund requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `subsection 20A(2) applies` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`subsection 20A(2) applies` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`subsection 20A(2) applies` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `subsection 20A(3) applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`subsection 20A(3) applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`subsection 20A(3) applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`subsection 20A(3) applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`subsection 20A(3) applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`subsection 20A(3) applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- 20B(2): every element, and a certificate provided no earlier than 15 months before 1 July 2026 (1 April 2025).
#ASSERT `subsection 20B(2) applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsection 20B(2) applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 4 2025) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsection 20B(2) applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 31 3 2025) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `subsection 20B(2) applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `subsection 20B(2) applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `subsection 20B(2) applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `subsection 20B(3) applies` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`subsection 20B(3) applies` FALSE)
#ASSERT `subsection 20B(4) applies` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`subsection 20B(4) applies` FALSE)

§ `Section 20C: the choice loading limit`

-- Notice period begun 1 July 2026, no notice that it has ended; current QE day 15 July 2026. An earlier QE day 2 July (1000) is in it; 30 June 2026 (500) is not.
`earlier contributions` MEANS LIST (`Earlier contribution subject to the choice loading` OF Date 2 7 2026, 1000), (`Earlier contribution subject to the choice loading` OF Date 30 6 2026, 500)
#ASSERT `the other eligible contributions within the notice period` (Date 1 7 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 7 2026) `earlier contributions` EQUALS 1000
-- The Commissioner's notice that the notice period had ended was given on 1 July 2026: 2 July is outside the period.
#ASSERT `the other eligible contributions within the notice period` (Date 1 7 2026) (JUST (Date 1 7 2026)) (Date 15 7 2026) `earlier contributions` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the other eligible contributions within the notice period` (Date 1 7 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 7 2026) EMPTY EQUALS 0
-- $1,200 reduced by 25% of the other contributions: 25% of 1000 is 250, so 950; 25% of 4800 is 1200, so nil; 25% of 5000 is 1250, so nil, not below it.
#ASSERT `the choice loading limit for the QE day` 0 EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `the choice loading limit for the QE day` 1000 EQUALS 950
#ASSERT `the choice loading limit for the QE day` 4800 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the choice loading limit for the QE day` 5000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the choice loading limit for the QE day` 4000 EQUALS 200

§ `Section 20A(1): the choice loading`

#ASSERT `the choice loading for the employee and the QE day` FALSE TRUE 1000 1200 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the choice loading for the employee and the QE day` TRUE FALSE 1000 1200 EQUALS JUST 0
-- 25% of 1000 is 250, below the limit of 1200.
#ASSERT `the choice loading for the employee and the QE day` TRUE TRUE 1000 1200 EQUALS JUST 250
-- 25% of 8000 is 2000, above the limit: the lower, 1200. 25% of 4800 is exactly 1200.
#ASSERT `the choice loading for the employee and the QE day` TRUE TRUE 8000 1200 EQUALS JUST 1200
#ASSERT `the choice loading for the employee and the QE day` TRUE TRUE 4800 1200 EQUALS JUST 1200
#ASSERT `the choice loading for the employee and the QE day` TRUE TRUE 4000 1200 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `the choice loading for the employee and the QE day` TRUE TRUE 4000 200 EQUALS JUST 200

§ `Section 16B: the superannuation guarantee shortfall`

#ASSERT `the total of the amounts` (LIST 1, 2, 3) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the total of the amounts` EMPTY EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `some amount is greater than nil` (LIST 0, 5)
#ASSERT NOT (`some amount is greater than nil` (LIST 0, 0))
#ASSERT NOT (`some amount is greater than nil` EMPTY)
-- A base shortfall of 700 for one employee: final 400, notional 20, uplift 60% of 420 = 252, no choice loading: 400 + 20 + 252 = 672.
#ASSERT `the superannuation guarantee shortfall of an employer for a QE day` (LIST 700) (LIST 0) (LIST 400) (LIST 20) 252 EQUALS JUST 672
-- Only a choice loading of 250 is greater than nil: the section applies; the total is 250.
#ASSERT `the superannuation guarantee shortfall of an employer for a QE day` (LIST 0) (LIST 250) (LIST 0) (LIST 0) 0 EQUALS JUST 250
-- Two employees: final shortfalls 400 and 100, notional components 20 and 5, uplift 315, loadings 0 and 50: 500 + 25 + 315 + 50 = 890.
#ASSERT `the superannuation guarantee shortfall of an employer for a QE day` (LIST 700, 200) (LIST 0, 50) (LIST 400, 100) (LIST 20, 5) 315 EQUALS JUST 890
-- No base shortfall and no choice loading greater than nil: section 16B does not apply.
#ASSERT `the superannuation guarantee shortfall of an employer for a QE day` (LIST 0) (LIST 0) (LIST 0) (LIST 0) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the superannuation guarantee shortfall of an employer for a QE day` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 30: arrangements to avoid payment`

#ASSERT `the employer is liable under section 30` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the employer is liable under section 30` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the employer is liable under section 30` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the employer is liable under section 30` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the amount of superannuation guarantee charge payable under section 30` TRUE 5000 EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `the amount of superannuation guarantee charge payable under section 30` FALSE 5000 EQUALS NOTHING
